{"data": {"Page": {"pageInfo": {"currentPage": 2, "hasNextPage": false}, "media": [{"id": 17623, "title": {"romaji": "Futago no Monchhichi", "english": null}, "format": "TV_SHORT", "description": "Monchichi-chan, the twin sister, loves her twin brother very much. She is a crybaby and always follows her brother. Monchichi-kun, the twin brother, protects his sister. He is a brave adventurer and a fishing champion but sometimes becomes a hasty boy. They enjoy wonderful and mysterious adventures together everyday.<br><br>\nWhen they take a space walk, they ride on a swan of the swan constellation and build a small house with aliens in the space. They can do everything children want to do and dream of.<br>\nThis heartwarming animation series featuring the pretty twins surely gives wonderful dreams, brother-sister love and hopes for the future to all the children in the world.<br><br>\n(Source: Production Reed)", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 2}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 8}, "season": "WINTER", "seasonYear": 1980, "episodes": 130, "duration": 5, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": null, "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Comedy"], "tags": [{"name": "Kids", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Episodic", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Animals", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 18283, "title": {"romaji": "Sonyeon 007 Eunhateukgongdae", "english": null}, "format": "MOVIE", "description": "A 1980 Korean Mecha movie from 007 franchise.", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 80, "countryOfOrigin": "KR", "source": null, "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Action", "Adventure", "Mecha", "Sci-Fi"], "tags": [{"name": "Space", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 18305, "title": {"romaji": "15 Sonyeon Uju Pyoryugi", "english": null}, "format": "MOVIE", "description": "A 1980 film about a group of children saving the galaxy.", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 70, "countryOfOrigin": "KR", "source": null, "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Action", "Sci-Fi"], "tags": [{"name": "Space", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 18321, "title": {"romaji": "Kkomaeosa Ttori", "english": null}, "format": "MOVIE", "description": "A 1980 Korean Fantasy movie.", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 70, "countryOfOrigin": "KR", "source": null, "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Action", "Adventure", "Drama", "Fantasy"], "tags": [{"name": "Historical", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Magic", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 18377, "title": {"romaji": "Ganbare!! Tabuchi-kun!! Gekitou Pennant Race", "english": null}, "format": "MOVIE", "description": "The Seibu Lions baseball team makes it to the next round of a baseball tournament thanks to the heroic efforts of its star player, Tabuchi, but the next stage will involve hard work and cooperation. In a sports anime that pitches caricatures of real-life players against cartoon characters, the Lions (whose real-life mascot is the grown-up Kimba the White Lion), keep losing games due to Tabuchi's poor condition-his shadow is getting paler. <br>\nA group of fellow players turns up at the stadium, accompanied by Dokaben, and they encourage Tabuchi to pull through. They organize a Tabuchi Day to show him how appreciated he is, but it is a miserable failure.<br>\nEventually, he is brought out of his depression by the arrival of a girl called Miyoko, who obliges by dressing up as a cheerleader.<br><br>\nNote: Real-life members of the Seibu Lions baseball team are caricatured.<br><br>\n(Source: AniDB)", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 5}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 5}, "season": "SPRING", "seasonYear": 1980, "episodes": 1, "duration": 95, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "MANGA", "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Comedy", "Sports"], "tags": [{"name": "Baseball", "rank": 20, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 19917, "title": {"romaji": "Nijuushi no Hitomi", "english": null}, "format": "SPECIAL", "description": "Based on the book by Tsuboi Sakae, which drew on her involvement in Japan's anarchist counterculture and opposition to Korean War rearmament.<br><br>\nCombined live action (handled by Akio Jissoji) and animation (handled by Shigetsugu Yoshida).<br>\nReleased as a TV special.<br><br>\n(Source: AniDB)", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 10}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 10}, "season": "FALL", "seasonYear": 1980, "episodes": 1, "duration": 70, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": null, "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Drama"], "tags": [{"name": "Historical", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 20199, "title": {"romaji": "Ganbare Gonbe", "english": null}, "format": "TV", "description": "Based on the long running (1958 to 1992) gag manga by Sonoyama Shuji.", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 4}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": 8}, "season": "SPRING", "seasonYear": 1980, "episodes": 77, "duration": 15, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": null, "hashtag": null, "genres": ["Comedy"], "tags": [{"name": "Parody", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}, {"name": "Kids", "rank": 50, "isAdult": false}]}, {"id": 102665, "title": {"romaji": "Sleepy", "english": null}, "format": "MOVIE", "description": "A Furukawa Taku film", "startDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "endDate": {"year": 1980, "month": null}, "season": null, "seasonYear": null, "episodes": 1, "duration": 5, "countryOfOrigin": "JP", "source": "ORIGINAL", "hashtag": null, "genres": [], "tags": []}, {"id": 102708, "title": {"romaji": "Crazy Monkey", "english": null}, "format": "MOVIE", "description": "Jackie Chan's 1979 film The Fearless Hyena opened in Japan a year later under the name Crazy Monkey accompanied with an independent original animated piece b